      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dividing Creek Historical Society, founded in 1982, is a volunteer group dedicated to preserving the area's history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/19286",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The society runs a museum and library that house artifacts and documents chronicling Dividing Creek’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/19286",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic sites under the society’s care include an old mill, a one‑room schoolhouse, and a blacksmith shop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/19286",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every year the society hosts a Harvest Festival and a summer concert series that draw locals and visitors alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/19286",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dividing Creek sits on County Route 553, 9.7 miles south‑southwest of Millville, and marks the southern end of Route 555.",
